guide.topic.quick.title = 5-minute quick start
guide.topic.quick.summary = If this is your first time, follow this short flow to capture the game, arrange what you need, and start the overlay.
guide.topic.quick.step.1 = Start Mabinogi, then select the game's Client.exe window from the window list at the top.
guide.topic.quick.step.2 = Try Auto capture first. Use Manual capture to select the game window yourself only when no game image appears.
guide.topic.quick.step.3 = Run quickslot detection, check the slots you want to use, and add them to the overlay.
guide.topic.quick.step.4 = In Manage Layout, set each element's position and size, then use Screen Preview to place the overlay on the actual monitor.
guide.topic.quick.step.5 = Start the overlay and check in the game that its position and size look the way you intended.
guide.topic.quick.tip = Saved slots are not loaded until Auto or Manual capture has run once. Capture the current game screen first.
guide.topic.capture.title = Profiles and window capture
guide.topic.capture.summary = Capture connects the current game screen to saved recognition positions. Your profile keeps those positions together with the related settings.
guide.topic.capture.step.1 = A profile stores the overlay layout, quickslot, buff, and Tuairim recognition positions, alerts, and hotkey timers.
guide.topic.capture.step.2 = Use Auto capture for normal use. If it cannot find the game, use Manual capture and select the Mabinogi window directly.
guide.topic.capture.step.3 = Before capture, leave every quickslot, the buff window, and the Tuairim gauge you plan to use visible. Covered UI cannot be recognized.
guide.topic.capture.step.4 = After moving the in-game UI or changing resolution or display scaling, capture again and run Validate saved slots to apply the new positions.
guide.topic.capture.tip = Even with the same profile, saved coordinates may no longer match after resolution, Windows scaling, or in-game UI placement changes.
guide.topic.quickslots.title = Quickslot detection and correction
guide.topic.quickslots.summary = Find quickslot groups in the captured screen and add only the slots you actually want in the overlay.
guide.topic.quickslots.step.1 = Start quickslot detection and drag a selection that contains one complete quickslot group.
guide.topic.quickslots.step.2 = If a candidate is slightly offset, select it and use dragging or the arrow keys to align it with the icon border.
guide.topic.quickslots.step.3 = For shapes automatic detection cannot handle, create a manual section or add a manual slot directly.
guide.topic.quickslots.step.4 = Check only the candidates you need and select Add slot. Added items appear in the slot list on the right.
guide.topic.quickslots.tip = Detect groups with different backgrounds, icon sizes, or spacing separately for better results.
guide.topic.layout.title = Overlay layout
guide.topic.layout.summary = Set the position, size, and opacity of overlay elements, as well as where the overlay window appears on your monitor.
guide.topic.layout.step.1 = Click an element and drag it or use the arrow keys. Hold Ctrl or Shift while clicking to select and move multiple elements together.
guide.topic.layout.step.2 = Set a grid size to snap new and moved elements into alignment. Group movement keeps the spacing between selected elements.
guide.topic.layout.step.3 = In Screen Preview, drag the top bar to move the whole overlay window. Enable position adjustment in preview to move individual elements there.
guide.topic.layout.step.4 = Select Save and close when finished. Cancel discards this editing session, while a reset cannot be undone.
guide.topic.layout.tip = If you moved quickslots or the buff window inside the game, also capture the new screen and run saved slot validation.
guide.topic.monitors.title = Buff and Tuairim alerts
guide.topic.monitors.summary = Recognize buffs and Tuairim first, then choose separately what to monitor, what to show in the overlay, and what sound to play.
guide.topic.monitors.step.1 = Capture a clear view of the buff window and Tuairim gauge, then run Buff window recognition and Tuairim UI recognition separately.
guide.topic.monitors.step.2 = O beside a buff means its icon position was found. X means it is not recognized yet and cannot be monitored even if selected.
guide.topic.monitors.step.3 = Select the buffs to monitor, then enable only the buff timer, Tuairim gauge, and alert display elements you want. Turn all display options off to use sound only.
guide.topic.monitors.step.4 = Set the alert point, frequency, sound file, and volume, then use Test to check the actual playback level.
guide.topic.monitors.tip = When combat effects briefly darken, brighten, or cover the buff window or Tuairim gauge, updates pause to avoid bad readings. Monitoring resumes automatically, but the timer may update a little late.
guide.topic.monitors.tuairim.tip = Tuairim alerts work only while the Tuairim gauge display is collapsed, with the Tuairim Boost percentage visible as a number.
guide.topic.timers.title = Hotkey timers
guide.topic.timers.summary = Press a chosen key while playing to start or reload a timer, and use a separate key to cancel it silently.
guide.topic.timers.step.1 = Add a timer and give it a recognizable name, full duration, and advance alert time.
guide.topic.timers.step.2 = Click the start or cancel hotkey field once, then press a single key or a Ctrl, Shift, or Alt combination.
guide.topic.timers.step.3 = Enable overlay display and sound as needed, and optionally choose a per-timer sound file and volume.
guide.topic.timers.step.4 = Start the overlay and test both keys while the game has focus. Pressing the start key again restarts the full duration.
guide.topic.timers.tip = If the game runs as administrator, a normally launched app may not receive its keys. Run Mabinogi Overlay as administrator only in that case.
guide.topic.erin.title = Erin Timer
guide.topic.erin.summary = See the current Erin time at a glance and receive sound or desktop alerts at selected Erin times.
guide.topic.erin.step.1 = If the app differs from the in-game clock, use time synchronization while looking at the game clock.
guide.topic.erin.step.2 = Set an alarm name and Erin time, then choose whether it repeats every day or rings only once.
guide.topic.erin.step.3 = Choose a common sound or a different sound for each alarm, then test the playback.
guide.topic.erin.tip = Compact mode also shows the current Erin time and lets you enable or disable individual alarms.
guide.topic.compact.title = Compact mode
guide.topic.compact.summary = After initial setup, switch to a smaller window that keeps only the controls you use frequently while playing.
guide.topic.compact.step.1 = Start or stop the overlay, and open Manage Layout directly whenever placement needs adjustment.
guide.topic.compact.step.2 = Toggle Buff and Tuairim monitoring and change which already recognized buffs are active.
guide.topic.compact.step.3 = Check hotkey timer countdowns, current Erin time, and registered Erin alarm states in one window.
guide.topic.compact.tip = Use Exit compact mode when you need to recognize new UI or change detailed alert values.
guide.topic.settings.title = Settings
guide.topic.settings.summary = Manage language and close behavior, multiple profiles, capture and renderer options, and app information in purpose-specific tabs.
guide.topic.settings.step.1 = Select a profile in the Profile tab and press Apply. A confirmation appears before replacing the current workspace.
guide.topic.settings.step.2 = The same tab can rename, save to file, load from file, or delete a profile. Deletion is permanent and requires two confirmations.
guide.topic.settings.step.3 = The General tab controls app language and Close behavior. You can change a previously remembered choice here.
guide.topic.settings.step.4 = Leave both capture and renderer on Automatic (recommended) for the most reliable setup. Use manual options only to troubleshoot a specific environment.
guide.topic.settings.tip = Changing the profile folder switches to the profiles in that folder. Save important profiles to a file before moving storage locations.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.title = Troubleshooting
guide.topic.troubleshooting.summary = Before rebuilding all your settings, start with the checks that match the symptom you are seeing.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.step.1 = If capture is blank or shows the wrong window, verify Client.exe and retry Auto capture. Use Manual capture or a manual backend only if it keeps failing.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.step.2 = If saved slots disappear or point to the wrong place, capture the current game screen and run Validate saved slots. Valid positions are applied to the profile immediately.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.step.3 = If a buff or Tuairim status shows X, make sure the complete UI is visible and not covered by another window or effect, then run recognition again.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.step.4 = If only in-game hotkeys fail, check duplicates and conflicts with other apps. If the game is elevated, the overlay may need the same permission level.
guide.topic.troubleshooting.tip = If the issue repeats, open the log from Settings and find the entries from the time it happened. Include the symptom, reproduction steps, and log in a GitHub Issue to make diagnosis much faster.
